- Time: \(O(n^2)\) worst case.
- Auxiliary space: \(O(h)\) for the recursion stack.
This avoids slicing, but we can still eliminate the repeated linear searches.

Approach 3 — Recursive Index Ranges + HashMap (Optimal)
This is the most common optimal recursive solution.
Idea
Build a HashMap once:
node value → inorder index


For the example:
9  → 0
3  → 1
15 → 2
20 → 3
7  → 4


Now the root's inorder position can be obtained in average \(O(1)\) time.

Everything else remains the same as Approach 2:
1. Root = last element of the current postorder range.
2. Use the map to get its inorder index.
3. Calculate the left subtree's size.
4. Recursively construct left and right children.
Code
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    public TreeNode buildTree(int[] inorder, int[] postorder) {

        Map<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < inorder.length; i++) {
            map.put(inorder[i], i);
        }

        return buildNode(
                inorder, 0, inorder.length - 1,
                postorder, 0, postorder.length - 1,
                map
        );
    }

    private TreeNode buildNode(
            int[] inorder,
            int inStart,
            int inEnd,
            int[] postorder,
            int postStart,
            int postEnd,
            Map<Integer, Integer> map) {

        if (inStart > inEnd || postStart > postEnd) {
            return null;
        }

        int rootVal = postorder[postEnd];
        TreeNode root = new TreeNode(rootVal);

        int rootIndex = map.get(rootVal);

        int leftSize = rootIndex - inStart;
        int rightSize = inEnd - rootIndex;

        root.left = buildNode(
                inorder,
                inStart,
                rootIndex - 1,
                postorder,
                postStart,
                postStart + leftSize - 1,
                map
        );

        root.right = buildNode(
                inorder,
                rootIndex + 1,
                inEnd,
                postorder,
                postEnd - rightSize,
                postEnd - 1,
                map
        );

        return root;
    }
}


